<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees March CPI at +0.2 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees March CPI at +0.2 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its March consumer price index stood at +0.2 percent month-on-month and +2.0 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In February, the Venice inflation rate was flat and 2.2 percent respectively. The general index and housing and utility charges sector have been revised to take account of a court ruling last month to suspend electricity tariff reductions.</p>
<p>Venice is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Thursday and Friday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.2     (0.0R)     2.0    (2.2R)</p>
<p>    Food				0.0    (-0.5)     -0.3    (0.4)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.6     (0.1)	3.9    (4.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges 0.2     (0.4R)     4.3    (4.5R)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.0     (0.1)	1.8    (1.9)</p>
<p>    Health services		-0.6     (0.3)	1.8    (2.6)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.4     (0.0)	2.8    (3.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  -0.3    (-0.1)     -2.3   (-1.9)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.0    (-3.5)	5.1    (2.3)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.6     (0.5)	6.1    (5.6)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services     0.2     (0.4)	0.6    (0.7)</p>
<p>R - revised</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
